{
  "requirement": "The Habeas Codicem project MUST keep its mdBook Markdown in `md/` and Rust source in `src/`, and its own book MUST use the Habeas preprocessor.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no gaps. Each of the requirement's three obligations has code that carries it out and a test that checks it.\n\n**Obligations and the code that carries them out**\n- **Markdown in `md/`:** `book.toml` `[book] src = \"md\"` (marked {impl}) sets the book source directory. `md/` holds `SUMMARY.md`, the chapters and the book's CSS.\n- **Rust source in `src/`:** `Cargo.toml` `[lib] path = \"src/lib.rs\"` and `[[bin]] path = \"src/main.rs\"` (both marked {impl}) place the library and binary roots in `src/`. `src/` holds the modules.\n- **The book uses the Habeas preprocessor:** `book.toml` `[preprocessor.habeas] command = \"cargo habeas mdbook\"` (marked {impl}) enables it. `.cargo/config.toml` defines the `habeas` alias that this command relies on.\n\n**Tests**\n- `tests/repository.rs::project_book_uses_the_repository_local_preprocessor_alias` is marked {test}. It asserts that `book.src` is `md`, that the preprocessor command is `cargo habeas mdbook`, and that the `habeas` alias exists. It also asserts that `md/SUMMARY.md`, `src/lib.rs` and `src/main.rs` exist.\n- `tests/repository.rs::crate_targets_are_declared_in_src` is marked {test}. It asserts that `lib.path` is `src/lib.rs` and that the only bin is `habeas` with path `src/main.rs`.\n\nI found no unspecified behavior and no FIXMEs.",
  "references": "015c9b5751983cb987f143849998916e726538b8a9f16fff4b9d8949fa828c13",
